  "note": "Election of the twelve councillors, polled Wednesday 17 May 1961 (the aldermen elected in 1958 were not due). All twelve official Unionists, sponsored by branches of the Central Armagh Unionist Association, were elected; Tom Newell, chairman of the Northern Ireland Labour Party and a councillor for nine years, lost his seat. Electorate 9,265; votes cast 5,316 (57.39 per cent); 63 spoilt."
